 "notes": "TN-4 left uncalled: Democrat Victoria Broderick leads Rep. Scott DesJarlais (R, D000616) by about 280 votes (0.14 pts) in unofficial Secretary of State totals and has claimed victory, but no AP call was found; Davidson County was to count remaining provisional ballots on Nov 16 and DesJarlais has not conceded. If she holds on she is a new member (2024 Democratic nominee for this seat). TN-9: AP called for Brent Taylor (49.6% to 48.5%) but Justin Pearson said he was not conceding. TN used a new 2026 map that split Memphis into districts 5, 8 and 9; district numbers above are the 2026 ones. SC-1: AP called for Lacore on Nov 6; margin 1.01 pts, just above SC automatic-recount threshold; Honeycutt's concession was not confirmed by her campaign. SC-2: Wilson's margin (0.99 pts) triggered a recount; WTOC reports the recount confirmed Wilson by 2,926 votes. SC-3 and SC-4 rest on one line in an SC Daily Gazette election-night article (opened only via search snippet; direct fetch was blocked), no vote totals found. SC-5: Climer's win confirmed by InvestmentNews and Wikipedia snippets; no vote totals found. MS-3: no district-level 2026 article found; 270toWin shows all 4 MS seats called (3 R, 1 D) and Guest was the only Republican on the MS-3 ballot (Ballotpedia), so Guest inferred as winner. AL-1: Jerry Carl is a former member (not in sitting roster). Alabama ran August special primaries under a changed map; results from Alabama Political Reporter, which did not state who called races. Several source pages (Ballotpedia, Axios, SC Daily Gazette, Tennessee Lookout) returned empty or 403 to direct fetch; some facts come from search-result summaries."
